From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] py/scheduler: Don't start a wait with a callback ready to run.

mp_event_wait_indefinite() and mp_event_wait_ms() handle pending events and
then wait, whatever the handling left behind. mp_handle_pending() runs at most
one Python callback, so a second one can stay queued with sched_state at
MP_SCHED_PENDING while the CPU sits in WFE. On rp2 that WFE returns only at the
next interrupt. mp_event_wait_ms() hides this for a short timeout, because
best_effort_wfe_or_timeout() adds an alarm, and so an event, when no alarm is
due sooner. It doesn't for a long timeout or at the friendly REPL.

On an RP2040 running an LVGL test app with three timers (10, 33 and 10 ms),
over 10 s, service timer callbacks:

    time.sleep_ms(500) in a loop:  747 before, 757 after
    time.sleep_ms(2000) in a loop: 359 before, 757 after
    time.sleep_ms(10000):           78 before, 754 after
    at the friendly REPL:          131 before, 728 after

Skip the wait while a callback this thread could run is ready. Ports still on
MICROPY_EVENT_POLL_HOOK, esp32 among them, don't reach this code.

diff --git a/py/scheduler.c b/py/scheduler.c
index 7849fcfe2..202359386 100644
--- a/py/scheduler.c
+++ b/py/scheduler.c
@@ -255,6 +255,23 @@ void mp_handle_pending(mp_handle_pending_behaviour_t behavior) {
     #endif
 }
 
+// Whether a wait should hold off, because the scheduler has a callback that this
+// thread could run now. mp_handle_pending() runs at most one Python callback at a
+// time, and the event that announced the next may have been used up already, so
+// nothing would wake the wait until some unrelated interrupt.
+static inline bool mp_event_callback_ready(void) {
+    #if MICROPY_ENABLE_SCHEDULER
+    #if MICROPY_PY_THREAD && !MICROPY_PY_THREAD_GIL
+    if (!mp_thread_is_main_thread()) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    #endif
+    return MP_STATE_VM(sched_state) == MP_SCHED_PENDING;
+    #else
+    return false;
+    #endif
+}
+
 // Handles any pending MicroPython events without waiting for an interrupt or event.
 void mp_event_handle_nowait(void) {
     #if defined(MICROPY_EVENT_POLL_HOOK_FAST) && !MICROPY_PREVIEW_VERSION_2
@@ -275,7 +292,9 @@ void mp_event_wait_indefinite(void) {
     MICROPY_EVENT_POLL_HOOK
     #else
     mp_event_handle_nowait();
-    MICROPY_INTERNAL_WFE(-1);
+    if (!mp_event_callback_ready()) {
+        MICROPY_INTERNAL_WFE(-1);
+    }
     #endif
 }
 
@@ -287,6 +306,8 @@ void mp_event_wait_ms(mp_uint_t timeout_ms) {
     MICROPY_EVENT_POLL_HOOK
     #else
     mp_event_handle_nowait();
-    MICROPY_INTERNAL_WFE(timeout_ms);
+    if (!mp_event_callback_ready()) {
+        MICROPY_INTERNAL_WFE(timeout_ms);
+    }
     #endif
 }
